Z||000000||varnster||09-22-2001||10:42 PM||||O.k I installed remote locks, starter and hatch system, only thing is the door locks<BR>dont want to unlock good when the engine is<BR>off. It trys I can hear it clicking and see<BR>the locks moving a little but it wont unlock.<BR>everything else works good, and when i start<BR>the car the locks work great! Its like it doesnt have enough power to unlock unless the<BR>car is running. I have a gell cell battery,<BR>and a high amp alt,I know the battery is good. thanks||||reg||8
Z||000001||rcn491||09-23-2001||12:26 AM||||If the wires are not a heavy enough gauge, you could be loosing enough voltage to cause your problem. Also check that the ground connection is good.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero_hunter85||09-23-2001||12:52 AM||||there are two other things i can think of. <BR>1.door lockes need to be lubed and 2. with the engine running there is alot more voltage because of the alternator but when the engine is off you only have the battery power. <BR>my 84 t/a does the same thing.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||09-23-2001||12:46 PM||||heres the solution, use remote starter to start it, then hit the remote locks. LOL||||reg||1
Z||000004||GTMike||09-23-2001||05:21 PM||||i'm going to be getting remote locks too. and i know i'm going to have the same problem because i have to hit my locks at least 2 times to get my driverside to lock all the way.  i think it just needs to be lubed up.  any suggestions?||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||09-23-2001||06:15 PM||||yes, there all getting on in years. the lube the factory put on all the linkages and locks is now turning to something resembling wax or tar. take off inside door panel and clean it all with WD40 or similar, then spray with some lithium lube. Will cure it almost all the time.||||reg||1
Z||000006||falconhulk||09-24-2001||02:12 PM||||Did you have power locks before installing the remote opener?  If so are you obtaining the power for the opener from the door lock circuit?  If not where are you tapping for power?  Where are you getting ground?  I have heard of this happening whne the battery has a bad ground to the chasis in older muscle cars.  When the alternator is in use then ground was better.  I have never seen this in person and doubt it would be the problem.  I would try obtaining power from a diffrent point and another ground.  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Alex2004||09-24-2001||04:22 PM||||I had that problem when i installed my keyless entry system except it wouldn't lock right w/ the ignition off. Mine is Bulldog keyless entry model 1402, anyways, they thought i wasn't getting enough voltage either, and i had check that, it was fine, check all the wires, they were fine, so they told me to send it back for service and they fixed it.  I would contact the manufacture and tell them what is going on, they should service it for you.  Hope that helps!  Mine works fine now!...<P>Alex...||||reg||4
Z||000008||varnster||09-24-2001||07:18 PM||||mine allso is a BULLDOG system good product<BR>at a good price except for this little problem I will check all connections and the ground THANKS!||||reg||14
